1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:02,247
Welcome to Night 5.

2
00:00:02,197 --> 00:00:08,726
Tonight we address the most common reason people with chronic insomnia stay awake at night.

3
00:00:08,726 --> 00:00:10,505
The racing mind.

4
00:00:10,505 --> 00:00:12,785
Here is what the research shows.

5
00:00:12,785 --> 00:00:16,549
The thoughts that surface at bedtime are not random.

6
00:00:16,550 --> 00:00:22,402
They are unprocessed tasks, unresolved worries, anticipated problems.

7
00:00:22,402 --> 00:00:26,402
Your brain has been holding them in working memory all day.

8
00:00:26,402 --> 00:00:32,932
When you stop the input, finally lying still in the dark, those held thoughts release.

9
00:00:32,932 --> 00:00:35,814
The solution is not to suppress them.

10
00:00:35,814 --> 00:00:38,226
Suppression makes them louder.

11
00:00:38,226 --> 00:00:42,755
The solution is to give them somewhere to go, before you lie down.

12
00:00:42,755 --> 00:00:51,285
This technique is called constructive worry, and it has the strongest evidence base of any sleep hygiene intervention.

13
00:00:51,285 --> 00:00:53,108
Here is the protocol.

14
00:00:53,108 --> 00:00:59,255
Fifteen minutes before your intended bedtime, sit at a table with a piece of paper.

15
00:00:59,255 --> 00:01:02,035
Divide the paper into two columns.

16
00:01:02,035 --> 00:01:05,564
On the left, write everything that is on your mind.

17
00:01:05,564 --> 00:01:11,549
Work, relationships, finances, anything pulling at your attention.

18
00:01:11,549 --> 00:01:17,123
On the right, write the single next step for each item, no matter how small.

19
00:01:17,123 --> 00:01:20,432
The act of writing the next step closes the loop.

20
00:01:20,432 --> 00:01:22,932
Your brain releases the thought.

21
00:01:22,932 --> 00:01:25,358
The paper goes into a drawer.

22
00:01:25,358 --> 00:01:27,902
The thoughts stay there until morning.

23
00:01:27,902 --> 00:01:30,094
They cannot follow you to the bed.

24
00:01:30,094 --> 00:01:33,152
Now, let go of the thoughts you wrote down.

25
00:01:33,152 --> 00:01:34,535
They are stored.

26
00:01:34,535 --> 00:01:36,932
You do not need to hold them anymore.

27
00:01:36,932 --> 00:01:40,138
Breathe in through your nose for four seconds.

28
00:01:40,138 --> 00:01:41,741
Hold for seven.

29
00:01:41,741 --> 00:01:43,902
Out through your mouth for eight.

30
00:01:43,902 --> 00:01:45,079
Again.

31
00:01:45,079 --> 00:01:46,549
In for four.

32
00:01:46,549 --> 00:01:48,152
Hold for seven.

33
00:01:48,152 --> 00:01:49,520
Out for eight.

34
00:01:49,520 --> 00:01:51,079
One last time.

35
00:01:51,079 --> 00:01:52,549
In for four.

36
00:01:52,549 --> 00:01:54,152
Hold for seven.

37
00:01:54,152 --> 00:01:55,520
Out for eight.

38
00:01:55,520 --> 00:01:57,844
Your mind is empty for the night.

39
00:01:57,844 --> 00:01:59,182
Sleep well.

